{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: recover the unfinished scale-envelope evidence outcome identified in #7454, after #20047. The original #2546 self-request and #5781 lane were retired with an explicit instruction to commission the remaining work on current bases. Their implementation children largely landed; the missing outcome is the broader target/evidence table, not another memory or checkpoint rewrite.\n\nCurrent [performance page](docs/reference/performance.md@1fba3d550091f720e48521bb89f222bd4c218af8:1) publishes the fan-out, fixed-append and 500k-memory lanes. The [versioned workload contract](performance/contract-v2.json@1fba3d550091f720e48521bb89f222bd4c218af8:1) already names actor counts 1/8/50 and tail-255 checkpoint cases at 50,000/500,000. The [limits page](docs/reference/limits.md@1fba3d550091f720e48521bb89f222bd4c218af8:188) keeps the 256 MiB checkpoint ceiling. There is no published two-envelope table covering the five remaining dimensions. See [history and current-source evidence](scale-envelope-recovery-evidence.json); [closed memory-lane accounting](scale-memory-closed-audit.json) confirms that its successor is satisfied and landed, with the three retained file hashes verified. Do not revive that completed implementation.\n\nDeliver the residual outcome:\n\n1. Before new timing, publish a versioned PREVIEW/FIRST-PRODUCTION target table in the working document: sequence depth, application-event count, actor count, dependency fan-out, checkpoint size, cold verify/restart, warm status and memory, with named hardware and reasons for each target. Reconcile the historical 50k/8-actor and 500k/50-actor envelopes against the current contract. Distinguish planning targets, measured capability and governing operational limits; a new production commitment or change to governed limits requires a concrete ordinary proposal and adoption first. Do not silently weaken a target to turn a miss into a pass.\n2. Complete the five residual dimensions: cold restart from an authenticated near-head checkpoint; cold verify without a checkpoint; warm-status latency; serialized checkpoint bytes; actor-count cost. Use the existing performance framework, preserving complete verification/fold semantics, signed identities, correctness checks and atomic publication. Retain exact source and harness heads, contract/fixture digests, raw samples, environment, ranges/distributions, case order and measurement windows under performance/retained/. Add only the bounded harness coverage needed for these cases. Separate axes do not prove the combined envelope: measure the joint cases needed for a claimed joint verdict or explicitly mark that verdict unmeasured.\n3. Reuse authenticated historical evidence as history. #6231/e2b15773 records the earlier checkpoint miss; #6292/7994ba10 records the later improvement. Check their actual heads and scope before publishing them. A historical measurement does not become a current-head result merely because the idea still exists. Avoid repeating expensive runs where existing exact evidence answers the claim; rerun when source or workload changes make it necessary. Coordinate a quiet measurement window with other workers, and report contention or insufficient samples honestly.\n4. Preserve the three already-published lanes, their actual measured revisions, and the fixed-append miss. Do not invent a new pass, discard unfavorable samples, turn harness correctness pass into target pass, or claim constant memory. Classify every new table result as measured, modeled, unavailable or inconclusive. Reconcile existing assignments before filing a bounded implementation child for each newly established miss; keep runtime optimizations out of this evidence delivery.\n5. Make performance.md and limits.md distinguish demonstrated preview behavior from any adopted production commitments. Check old task-status sentences against the current fold. Publish behavior-grounded exact-path artifacts for the complete delivery, get fresh independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review, ratify approval, seal the main merge, push, check CI and remove the owned worktree/branch.\n\nUse request/scale-envelope-evidence from then-current main, after the current queue. Do not run a full timing campaign in default CI, interrupt I7/reviews, change repository-admin controls (#8162 stays deferred), or restart/reset real services. Inherited ordinary staleness alone does not require refiling. If a later durable owner for this exact residual is found, reconcile it with this request before duplicating work.","body":{"branch":"request/scale-envelope-evidence","conditions":"Complete the remaining two-envelope scale target/evidence table and five residual dimensions from #7454, preserving delivered evidence lanes and existing policy, with independent exact-head review and sealed main delivery.","head":"1fba3d550091f720e48521bb89f222bd4c218af8","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0c85f097e94681a79024bcf284260256919d2530, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2e39279f58ab90c8808dcc05623cdf57e3f25ca4, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2f7ef45ac738cedc99aac0c20df4e2e22b2a2e64, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:56c0e84d7115c2695fb92a8715268d42aedba8f7 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:00925ae6c09fb0b8e2a72e84c22ca3488bc9534d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:063ac469f4327eef88a6cef497d6b24b5d128af7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:069ba281df08c36e7b19c66532ae24357887a9e5, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0953bfe693cd591ec4cd901025bc29c9047e27d2 and 60 more","target_head":"1fba3d550091f720e48521bb89f222bd4c218af8","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}